          <td colspan="2" height="30" background="newsheader.jpg"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b><font size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Vindi & Statue Dead - Other Ubermobs Quake in Fear</font></b></font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr bgcolor="#330033"> 
          <td width="60%"><font size="2"><i><font face="Verdana">by <A href="javascript:createWindow('memberdetails.asp?id=1','profile','scrollbars,width=550,height=500')"><font color=yellow>Falqour Thornwalker</font></a></font></i></font></td>
          <td width="40%"> 
            <div align="right"><font size="2"><b>Posted: 4/8/2002 3:54:38 AM</b></font></div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td colspan="2">
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><B>...no, not the Plane of Fear, just regular old fear. SoF puts to rest two of Kael Drakkel's more vile residents - and yes, they got pictures...                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       </B></font><P>
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="5">The Fall of Kael Drakkel</font></p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2">The Spirits of Fire descended upon Kael Drakkel, city of the hated Kromzek - the Storm Giants of Rallos Zek - in their first attempt at destroying Derekor the Vindicator, a particularly vile creature who has been charged with numerous atrocities committed against the Dragons of the Claws of Veeshan, the peaceful Coldain Dwarves, as well as the Tunarian Court itself. Below is a photo log of the days events.</font></p><p align="center"> </p><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th1.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">The Vindicator is Slain</font><br><b>Justice has been served</b><br>(Center: Derekor_the_Vindicator`s_corpse00)</font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th2.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Why Did I Take This Picture?</font><br><b>I forgot.. Well, it's sorta interesting.. There's the Vindicator's feet over in the corner.. Some people standing around...</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th3.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Where's a_Waldo01</font><br><b>Are you in this picture? Take a close look... Grats to everyone who help in the Vindi slaying!</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th4.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Where's a_Waldo02</font><br><b>If you weren't in the picture above, maybe you're in this one.</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th5.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Did You Hear Something?</font><br><b>Uh oh! It looks like The Statue of Rallos Zek has become angry with the Spirits of Fire! Oh well, we can fix that...</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th6.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">The Corpse of The Statue of Rallos Zek</font><br><b>Another SoF First! The Statue of Rallos Zek is slain in our first attempt.</b><br>(Foreground: Mckenna / Foreground: Mckenna / Foreground: Mckenna... I need to stop looking at Mckenna... Background: Something that isn't Mckenna)</font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th7.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Cleanup Time</font><br><b>The fallen loot their own corpses and find all sorts of uber gear!</b><br>(Foreground: Lucane, ubertank)</font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th8.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Nobody Tosses a Dwarf</font><br><b>Rayder did a great job of tanking after Lucy ate it</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th9.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">Nobody Photographs a Dwarf</font><br><b>Snackish tells you, "There better not be film in that thing."</b></font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="2"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/april7th10.jpg" width="500" height="375"><br><font size="5">More Corpse Cleanup</font><br><b>Photo worthy? Maybe not. But, Mckenna was sitting down, so, not much else to do.</b><br>(Foreground left: Krystof / Background Center: Haletma / Background Right: Matthi / Foreground Right: A_Dead_Quixie06)</font></p><hr><p align="center"><font face="Verdana" size="3">Once again, grats to everyone who participated in these two historic SoF firsts! And, grats to those who got loot!</font></p>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             </font>
</td>
